From: tabS3 bring-up <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: camss: vote for the VFE's memory path on MSM8996

The VFE writes its frames through the multimedia NOC, a path the RPM
only keeps clocked while somebody votes bandwidth on it. The MSM8996
resources carry no interconnect paths, so the camera only works while
the display is on, whose bandwidth vote keeps the path alive. With the
panel blanked (SM-T825 running Debian, 60 s idle) the VFE still receives
every frame (its SOF interrupts keep coming) but none of its writes
complete: no buffer is ever returned, the halt at stream-off times out
("VFE halt timeout") and the VFE SMMU then fails every TLB sync ("TLB
sync timed out -- SMMU may be deadlocked") until a reboot.

Add the two paths MSM8953 already votes for, a config path and the VFE's
path to DDR, so the driver requests bandwidth while the block is in use.
The device tree names them "cam_ahb" and "cam_vfe_mem".

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5-1
---
diff -ruN a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c	2026-10-14 12:00:50.458295504 +0300
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c	2026-10-14 12:00:50.458413519 +0300
@@ -308,6 +308,19 @@
 	},
 };
 
+static const struct resources_icc icc_res_8x96[] = {
+	{
+		.name = "cam_ahb",
+		.icc_bw_tbl.avg = 38400,
+		.icc_bw_tbl.peak = 76800,
+	},
+	{
+		.name = "cam_vfe_mem",
+		.icc_bw_tbl.avg = 939524,
+		.icc_bw_tbl.peak = 1342177,
+	},
+};
+
 static const struct camss_subdev_resources csiphy_res_8x96[] = {
 	/* CSIPHY0 */
 	{
@@ -4319,6 +4332,8 @@
 	.csid_res = csid_res_8x96,
 	.ispif_res = &ispif_res_8x96,
 	.vfe_res = vfe_res_8x96,
+	.icc_res = icc_res_8x96,
+	.icc_path_num = ARRAY_SIZE(icc_res_8x96),
 	.csiphy_num = ARRAY_SIZE(csiphy_res_8x96),
 	.csid_num = ARRAY_SIZE(csid_res_8x96),
 	.vfe_num = ARRAY_SIZE(vfe_res_8x96),
